<%#
  "Participants from a file", all of it, on one page.

  Two states of the same screen, not two screens:

    no file yet   → `_upload`: the file field and what the file needs.
    file read     → `_review`: what we understood, what we could not, who
                    will be able to vote, and the button that imports.

  The second state is reached by a redirect back here with the uploaded
  file's signed id (`?blob=`), so a refresh cannot re-post the upload, and
  anything wrong with the rows is reported here too rather than on a page of
  its own.

  `@upload_form` is a CensusFileUploadForm, `@form` a CensusFileMappingForm
  (nil until a file is read), `@outcome` the rows' problems when an import
  was refused.
%>
<% scope = "decidim.elections.vocdoni.admin.census_file.new" %>
<% add_decidim_page_title(t("title", scope:)) %>
<% append_javascript_pack_tag "decidim_elections_vocdoni_admin" %>
<% append_stylesheet_pack_tag "decidim_elections_vocdoni_admin", media: "all" %>
<% reviewing = @form.present? && @form.reader.present? %>

<div class="item_show__header border-none">
  <h1 class="item_show__header-title"><%= t("title", scope:) %></h1>
</div>

<%= render "decidim/elections/admin/elections/tabs_menu" %>

<div class="vocdoni-census-file">
  <% if reviewing %>
    <%= render "decidim/elections/vocdoni/admin/census_file/review", form: @form, outcome: @outcome %>
  <% else %>
    <%= render "decidim/elections/vocdoni/admin/census_file/upload", form: @upload_form %>
  <% end %>
</div>
